<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">5 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 5 May, from 1215 to 1961.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1215">1215 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">811 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rebel barons renounce their allegiance to King John</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A group of English barons formally withdrew their fealty from John and took up arms. Their capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> weeks later forced the king to agree to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magna-carta">Magna Carta</a> in June.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1789">1789 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">237 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Estates-General opens at Versailles</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xvi">Louis XVI</a> convened the Estates-General for the first time since 1614 to resolve a financial crisis. Disputes over voting led the Third Estate to declare itself the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-assembly-of-france">National Assembly</a> in June.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1821">1821 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">205 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon dies in exile on St Helena</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a> died aged 51 on the remote Atlantic island where the British had held him since 1815. His legal code and the states he redrew outlived his empire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1835">1835 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">191 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Continental Europe's first passenger railway opens in Belgium</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Trains began running between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> and Mechelen on the first state-built passenger line on the European mainland. Newly independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> soon had a national rail network.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1862">1862 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">164 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mexican army defeats the French at Puebla</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">General Ignacio <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a>'s outnumbered troops repulsed a French assault on Puebla. The victory, marked as Cinco de Mayo, delayed but did not prevent the French occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1891">1891 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">135 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tchaikovsky helps open New York's Music Hall, later Carnegie Hall</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Andrew Carnegie's new concert hall opened with a festival at which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyotr-ilyich-tchaikovsky">Tchaikovsky</a> conducted. Renamed Carnegie Hall in 1893, it became America's most famous concert venue.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1961">1961 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">65 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alan Shepard becomes the first American in space</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Alan Shepard made a 15-minute suborbital flight in Freedom 7, three weeks after Gagarin's orbit. Twenty days later President Kennedy committed the US to landing a man on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a>.</p></div></li></ol>
